Google DeepMind's AlphaFold predicted the 3D structure of virtually all 200 million known proteins — a problem that had stumped biochemists for 50 years — opening a new era in drug discovery.
A 2020 study in Nature found AI detected breast cancer from mammograms with 11.5% fewer false positives and 2.7% fewer false negatives than trained radiologists.
AI-powered sepsis alert systems in hospitals have reduced sepsis mortality by 18% by detecting deterioration hours before clinical signs become obvious to human staff.
IBM Watson for Genomics identifies tumour mutations and matches them to targeted therapies in minutes; manual genomic analysis takes days — in oncology, speed translates directly to survival.
